            <div xml:id="d190-a4-a14">

                <pb facs="0456" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg332"/>

                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ah Sing</hi> (through Chee Quong,
                    interpreter):</p>
                <p>I live at the corner of Nineteenth and Lawrence. I keep a wash-house. I was in
                    the house last Sunday evening when the mob came, and I was lying under the
                    ironing-table. I saw the parties, but could not recognize them as it was dark. I
                    did not see them take out Sing Lee, as the mob put a rope around my neck and
                    dragged me out of the house, but it was so dark I could not see them to identify
                    them. Sing Lee was in the house at the time the mob entered the house. The mob
                    cut off my cue after they got me outside of the house. I could not identify any
                    of the prisoners if I should look at them. They took me out before they seized
                    Sing Lee.</p>
                <closer><signed>CHEE QUONG.</signed></closer>
            </div>
